# Implementation Plan - Production-Ready SaaS Backend Migration

This plan details the steps to transition the Clip Submission System from a single-instance development mock (using SQLite databases and in-process queues) to a production-grade, highly-scalable architecture running on PostgreSQL and Redis (BullMQ).

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Hosting & Infrastructure Dependencies**:
> Running this configuration requires:
> 1. **PostgreSQL Database** (e.g., Neon or standard Postgres).
> 2. **Redis Database** (e.g., Railway Redis or Redis Cloud) for BullMQ queues and rate-limiting.
>
> We will configure the backend to automatically fall back to mocking databases/queues if the environment variables are not present in development, but production requires setting these variables.

